WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.650
To find the origin of Valak, the most feared
demon in the Conjurverse lore to date, we

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:08.290
must look to the legends passed down in one
small town in Romania.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:12.700
The tales tell of a Duke in the dark ages,
which puts us somewhere between 500 and 1000

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.700
CE.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.930
He built a great castle, which would later
be known as the Abbey of St. Carta.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:20.699
Hidden in the dungeons was a summoning ground,
carved with the serpentine symbol of a mythical

00:00:20.699 --> 00:00:22.609
being known as Valak.

00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:26.070
The people in the town feared the Duke, because
he wrote countless texts on witchcraft and

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.540
rituals to call upon these evil forces of
hell.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.970
He would eventually use these spells to open
the gateway between our world and the underworld.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:37.200
By sacrificing five people as a part of his
spell, the Duke would allow Valak to come

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.100
through, and walk amongst the living.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.580
But as Valak rose through the crevices, the
church, who had caught wind of the foul things

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.570
happening there, stormed the castle and interrupted
the liturgy.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:49.670
They attempted to seal the gateway using liquid
from the holy grail, and while this appeared

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:53.330
to cause the portal to close back up, this
seal would not last forever.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:57.520
To learn the secrets of Valak’s past, the
entity’s true purpose, what it represents

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:02.090
for the story and the character’s future,
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.630
Welcome to Horror History.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:10.746
My name is Professor CZsWorld, and you better
pay attention this time you little piece of sh-

00:01:10.746 --> 00:01:14.539
In today’s lesson we’re going over what
I consider to be the main boss of the Conjuring

00:01:14.539 --> 00:01:15.245
franchise.

00:01:15.245 --> 00:01:19.189
Like it’s counterpart Malthus, from the
Annabelle spin-offs, Valak is based on a mythological

00:01:19.189 --> 00:01:23.200
deity from The Lesser Key of Solomon, a series
of grimoires on demonology.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:28.180
It’s divided into five books, one of which
is called Ars Goetia, a textbook guide to

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.439
conjuring demons.

00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:33.119
In Annabelle, Ars Goetia was replaced with
this textbook called The Devil’s Welcome,

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:36.619
but to learn about Valak, we need to turn
the clock back even further, and look into

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:41.545
the pages of these mysterious texts found
in a tomb just outside the Abbey of St. Carta.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:50.030
When the ancient books are discovered, we
can see the outer cover of three of them.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:54.399
Two of them have piercing, yellow, serpentine
eyes, much like the eyes of Valak and anyone

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:56.229
else the demon takes control of.

00:01:56.229 --> 00:02:00.583
This suggests that these books, unlike The
Devil’s Welcome, may specifically be about Valak.

00:02:00.583 --> 00:02:04.820
The snake eating its own tail symbol is commonly
associated with Valak in the movie, but I’ll

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.020
come back to that shortly.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:10.539
In Ars Goetia, there are 72 demons said to
have been commanded by The Israeli King Solomon.

00:02:10.539 --> 00:02:15.879
They range from Kings, Dukes, Princes, Marquises,
Knights, Presidents, and Earls.

00:02:15.879 --> 00:02:17.659
Valak is considered a President of Hell.

00:02:17.659 --> 00:02:21.269
In the mythology, Valak looks a lot different
than it does in The Conjuring movies, but

00:02:21.269 --> 00:02:25.525
there are some references to the mythological
version that you may not have noticed in the movies.

00:02:25.525 --> 00:02:29.219
On one page of the book, there is a boy-like
form with a snake coming out of its mouth.

00:02:29.219 --> 00:02:32.690
This is likely a reference to how Valac is
depicted in The Lesser Key of Solomon, as

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.540
an angelically winged boy riding on a two
headed dragon.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:39.220
In the movies, Valak is a shapeshifter, whose
form seems to change based on what makes its

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.500
victims most uncomfortable.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.120
There’s also this image.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.640
Valak is commonly associated with a snake.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.939
Serpent symbols can be found throughout the
monastery and there are multiple occasions

00:02:47.939 --> 00:02:52.610
where the demon is introduced as Valak, the
defiler, the profane, the marquis of snakes.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:56.870
The bird is probably there to represent Malphas,
an Earl of Hell in mythology who you may know

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:58.799
as the demon that is connected to the Annabelle
doll.

00:02:58.799 --> 00:03:02.170
I did an entire video on the history of Malthus
if you’re interested.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:06.280
That would leave the question of who these
other two horned demons are… perhaps other

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.640
villains that we’ll meet in future Conjuring
movies.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:12.489
On another page, you’ll see a more familiar
sight, the Nun form of Valak, which seems

00:03:12.489 --> 00:03:15.959
to be it’s favorite form to use, but there
may be a reason that we see the Nun form so

00:03:15.959 --> 00:03:16.959
often.

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:19.909
On the side, you’ll notice another picture
of a snake eating its own tail.

00:03:19.909 --> 00:03:23.849
This is known as an Ouroboros, a mark seen
in many ancient cultures as a symbol for the

00:03:23.849 --> 00:03:25.540
cycle of life, death, and rebirth.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:30.069
We don’t exactly know what Valak’s endgame
is, but we know it has a strong desire to

00:03:30.069 --> 00:03:32.579
possess, as explained in The Conjuring 2.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:36.790
Perhaps by possessing someone and moving into
a new body, Valak feels a sense of new life,

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:40.370
and the ouroboros is a sign of the tendency
to go from body to body, creating a cycle

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:41.999
of new demonic possessions.

00:03:41.999 --> 00:03:45.799
The text written in the book isn't legible,
but Father Burke does read some of it aloud,

00:03:45.799 --> 00:03:48.030
and I am going to roll it.

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.139
So roll it.

00:03:50.177 --> 00:03:56.340
FATHER BURKE : “...And out of the ground…
formed every beast of the field and every

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:59.037
bird of the sky.

00:03:59.037 --> 00:04:06.000
Whatever the man called a living creature,
that was its name.

00:04:06.881 --> 00:04:08.331
Valak.”

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:12.420
This passage is part of the biblical text
of Genesis 2:19, so I looked up the meaning

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.760
of that passage and found the following:

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.030
“The act of naming something is meaningful
in the book of Genesis.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:20.610
This act often implies rule over and responsibility
for that thing."

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:24.620
This may explain why Lorraine is eventually
able to defeat Valak but we'll get there when

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:25.620
we get there.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:29.670
Now you may be thinking, this Valak guy sounds
like kind of a bad dude, going around possessing

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:32.520
people and crap, who would actually want to
summon Valak?

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:36.590
If we go back to the mythological readings
of Ars Goetia, it describes the benefits of

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:38.560
calling upon this malevolent force.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:43.000
He perfectly locates hidden treasure and finds
where serpents may be hiding, which he delivers

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.740
into the hands of the Conjurer.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:49.040
Valak is void of any force or strength, but
has dominion over 30 legions of devils.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.830
If this holds true to the Conjuring version
of Valak, it explains why The Duke of St.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:56.921
Carta built this fortress and tried so hard
to summon Valak there, he was driven by the

00:04:56.921 --> 00:04:58.750
allure of power and riches.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:02.780
The book also associates a sigil, or a symbol
considered to have magical power, to each

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:03.780
of the 72 demons.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:07.740
If you’ve seen Hereditary, you may recognize
the necklace as an example of this.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.750
They don’t lean too hard on this in The
Conjuring, but I did notice that the summoning

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:14.430
ground inside the Abbey almost seems to resemble
the sigil of Valak.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:18.586
But upon closer inspection, the outer ring
is formed by a double-ouraboros.

00:05:18.586 --> 00:05:21.980
This image can also be seen in one of the
other books, next to a more traditional demonic

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:23.630
form resembling a gargoyle.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:27.360
I’ve always assumed that this is Valak’s
true form, because it’s also seen labeled

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.539
as Valak on another page, and it seems to
be the form used when Valak enters and eventually

00:05:31.539 --> 00:05:32.570
exits our world.

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:36.789
That brings me back to the summoning ritual,
which, as I mentioned, was thwarted by the

00:05:36.789 --> 00:05:37.789
church.

00:05:37.789 --> 00:05:39.729
They took over the castle and converted it
into the abbey.

00:05:39.729 --> 00:05:43.669
The place was fully surrounded by crosses
to keep the evil contained, and nuns prayed

00:05:43.669 --> 00:05:47.490
there continuously, working in shifts so that
the place was constantly being blessed.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:52.009
Earlier I called Valak the main boss of The
Conjuring franchise, and this is why.

00:05:52.009 --> 00:05:56.069
Malthus, from the Annabelle movies, is considered
one of the most powerful supernatural entities,

00:05:56.069 --> 00:05:59.470
but in order to keep it contained, the Warrens
have a priest come twice a month to bless

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:00.470
the room.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:04.599
To keep Valak contained, however, several
nuns have to work together 24/7, and even

00:06:04.599 --> 00:06:07.700
this is only enough to hold the demon off
for so long.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:11.610
One of them describes the bombs of war shaking
the Abbey and once again cracking open the

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:12.610
gateway.

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:15.669
I’m guessing that this was during World
War II, and Romania was subject to air raids

00:06:15.669 --> 00:06:16.669
during that war.

00:06:16.669 --> 00:06:21.389
Romania was hit with air raids in 1943 and
1944, less than a decade before the main events

00:06:21.389 --> 00:06:23.759
of The Nun, which takes place in 1952.

00:06:23.759 --> 00:06:28.510
But ever since those bombs dropped, an unidentified
nun began stalking the corridors of the abbey

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:29.510
at night.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:31.892
But this nun was anything but holy.

00:06:40.819 --> 00:06:44.449
As perhaps the most powerful entity in the
world of The Conjuring, with the ability to

00:06:44.449 --> 00:06:49.250
take on any form, why does Valak so often
choose to become a simple nun?

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:52.949
Why not a creepy clown, a mummy or Coraline’s
mom?

00:06:52.949 --> 00:06:55.050
The answer lies in its setting.

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.550
“It’s something unholy.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:07:00.389
It takes on different forms to deceive us
and prey on our weaknesses.”

00:07:00.389 --> 00:07:04.270
Valak uses the Nun form to blend in with the
order, and eventually purge or corrupt each

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.270
of them.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.940
This could be the reason that the nuns are
generally never supposed to leave the Abbey,

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.000
so that they cannot be a vessel for Valak’s
escape.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.849
It was likely just after Valak was released, but before they realized Valak was

00:07:13.849 --> 00:07:16.970
among them and locked the place down, when
Sister Charlotte visited the Abbey.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:20.599
While she doesn’t personally encounter Valak,
she does have kind of a close call, since

00:07:20.599 --> 00:07:22.870
it seems to appear in the background of her
photo.

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:26.910
One by one, Valak picks off each of the remaining
nuns until only two remain.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:30.560
They go into the dungeon area where the gateway
is, to try to retrieve a relic that they believe

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:34.440
will save them, but when Valak quickly strikes
down the elder of the two, the lone survivor

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:38.580
must give herself up so that the demonic presence
does not have a vessel to escape in.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:42.389
Not long after, a delivery guy named Maurice,
most people just call him Frenchie, discovers

00:07:42.389 --> 00:07:46.259
the remains and word gets around to the Vatican
that trouble is afoot in Romania.

00:07:46.259 --> 00:07:50.000
They send one of their best priests, Father
Burke, and an inexperienced novitiate,

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:53.190
or nun-training, named Irene Palmer to investigate.

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:57.259
Valak watches them as they arrive, and somehow,
the scene of the incident is still fresh.

00:07:57.259 --> 00:08:00.949
Valak continues to haunt the premises, but
the ghosts of the nuns that inhabited it still

00:08:00.949 --> 00:08:01.949
linger.

00:08:01.949 --> 00:08:04.969
So when Sister Irene and Father Burke speak
to the Reverend Mother, the highest ranking

00:08:04.969 --> 00:08:09.250
nun in the convent, I’m assuming that this
is actually Valak posing as the Reverend Mother,

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:11.789
because the throne she’s sitting on has
an Ouroboros on it.

00:08:11.789 --> 00:08:14.840
She tells them that the nuns are about to
take a vow of silence for the evening, but

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.969
they can stay over and speak to them in the
morning.

00:08:16.969 --> 00:08:20.720
This may be part of Valak’s plan to try
to eliminate Burke and possess Irene during

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:21.387
the night.

00:08:21.387 --> 00:08:25.419
As Frenchie heads back to the town after escorting
them, Valak uses a variety of scary forms

00:08:25.419 --> 00:08:28.296
to send him running, so that he’s unlikely
to want to come back for them.

00:08:28.296 --> 00:08:29.590
Including this thing.

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:33.180
If we’re doing spin-offs on every character
that appears, we gotta do this guy.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:37.340
Burke is awoken by what appears to be a boy
he performed a failed exorcism on years ago.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:40.810
When he catches up to him, a snake slithers
out of the boy’s mouth and comes for Burke,

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:45.000
knocking him back into an open casket which
becomes instantly buried by Valak’s magic.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.700
Next, Sister Irene is lured out of bed into
the chapel, where she sees the demon’s shadow

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:53.310
circle around her until it gets to the mirror,
and appears in a corporeal form behind her,

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:57.120
but only in the reflection, before it roars
at her and shatters the mirror.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.340
Valak appeared to them each in different forms,
because it represents that which they have

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:01.340
yet to overcome.

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:05.150
For Burke, he hasn’t stopped feeling guilty
about the child he was unable to save, so

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:07.810
Valak appears as that child to prey on his
weakness.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:11.000
For Irene, it appears as the nun, because
she hasn’t made the commitment to take her

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.000
vows yet.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.630
They are each confronted by a challenge they
have yet to overcome.

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:18.630
Irene hears the bell ringing in the graveyard,
signifying that Burke had been buried alive,

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:19.940
and was using his lifeline.

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:23.830
You should learn from his example, and when
you do make sure you hit ALL notifications.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.920
The next morning, they come back to speak
with the nuns, not realizing that there are

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.070
none remaining.

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:29.640
Like, N-O-N-E none.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:33.260
I assume that Valak is the one to open the
gate for them, and probably also the one to

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:36.660
close it that evening, locking Irene inside
for another night.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:40.760
As Father Burke studies the map, Valak, this
time posing as the Abbess, tells him he won’t

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.590
find another way in.

00:09:43.862 --> 00:09:46.550
“It’s too late, Father.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:50.520
Sister Irene is lost.”

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:54.220
This also plays into Burke’s fears, because
he doesn’t want Sister Irene to be the latest

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:56.120
person he was unable to save.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:59.550
Valak grabs him using the same decrepit hands
that attacked him when he was trapped in the

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:01.590
coffin, and they break off and crumble on
the floor.

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:05.470
He also encounters a zombified version of
the boy that’s been haunting him, as demonic

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:06.940
hands protrude from the walls.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:11.270
When he reaches him, he has Valak’s signature
yellow eyes and forked tongue, a trait commonly

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:12.740
associated with the devil.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:16.490
Burke breaks free and runs for it, probably
narrowly avoiding being possessed, and when

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:20.380
he looks back, the ancient evil has reverted
to it’s unnerving nun form.

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:23.980
Meanwhile, Irene awakes from a nightmare and
discovers a door that’s labeled “Finit

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:25.980
Hic Deo”, or “God Ends Here.”

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:30.530
She too encounters Valak, who creates a turbulent
windstorm in the hallway and… you already

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:31.530
know what’s coming.

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:35.440
She gets air yeeted across the hall, but she’s
rescued by the ghost of Sister Oana and joins

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:38.070
the others in a little midnight emergency
prayer sesh.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:42.290
This is probably a scene that took place at
some point in the 1940s just after Valak had

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:45.490
begun coming after the lives of these nuns,
and we’re just seeing a slightly altered

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:49.840
version of it that includes Sister Irene -- but
since I don’t know that 100%, I’m keeping

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:50.840
it here in the chronology.

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:54.500
I’m also not really clear on if the prayers
of the ghost nuns would actually help hold

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:58.220
the seal at all, but we can at least say that
them encouraging Sister Irene to pray would

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:01.030
have some effect, because Sister Irene is
real.

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:04.290
It doesn’t come without cost though, because
Valak makes like that goth girl you dated

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:06.920
in college and scratches a pentagram into
her back.

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:10.440
Burke and Frenchie team up against a re-animated
version of Sister Victoria.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:14.020
Based on what we know from Ed and Lorraine’s
various lectures, this isn’t a possession,

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:17.270
because the demon would need a soul in order
to possess someone, and that would defeat

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:18.990
the purpose of Sister Victoria’s sacrifice.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:22.680
So what’s probably going on here is that
Valak is just moving around her body, the

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:24.880
same way that Malthus moves around the Annabelle
doll.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:27.760
“It was moved around to give the impression
of possession.”

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:31.310
Anyway, they catch up with Sister Irene, who
finally realizes the nuns she’s been talking

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:32.810
to were only an apparition.

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:34.100
“There’s no one left.

00:11:34.746 --> 00:11:36.356
We have our answer Father.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:40.036
As if there was any doubt before, this place
is no longer holy.”

00:11:40.036 --> 00:11:44.590
Valak next encounters them in the dungeon
area beyond the door with the Latin text translating

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:45.980
to God Ends Here.

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:49.630
This area represents Hell within the monastery,
so it is fitting that this should be where

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:51.920
their final battle with Valak takes place.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:55.688
They split up to search for the gate… because,
you know, that’s the best plan in a horror movie.

00:11:55.688 --> 00:11:59.280
Sister Irene enters one of the rooms, and
Valak appears in the form of a… what’s

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:00.920
the word for a group of nuns?

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.200
A horde?

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.200
A flock?

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:06.250
OK, I looked it up, apparently it’s called a superfluity.

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:09.170
Which was definitely not the word I was looking
for, but whatever.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:10.950
We’ll just call it a crowd of Nuns.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:15.200
Each of them has their faces covered, and
they’re able to overcome Irene and possess

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:15.711
her.

00:12:15.711 --> 00:12:16.887
“You failed.

00:12:17.474 --> 00:12:21.215
Just as you failed everyone in your life.

00:12:21.215 --> 00:12:24.756
Tomorrow a village will be missing its idiot.”

00:12:33.497 --> 00:12:37.250
Irene’s apparent possession does not last
long, as Frenchie kicks down the door and

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:40.904
encounters the possessed Irene, who air yeets
him into a pillar.

00:12:44.094 --> 00:12:47.910
We’ve seen a lot of air yeeting in this
franchise, and really just this era of horror

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:50.510
in general, but that one looks kind of painful.

00:12:53.016 --> 00:12:57.490
However, Sister Irene still has the holy grail
hanging around her neck, and Frenchie is able

00:12:57.490 --> 00:13:01.150
to smear some of it onto Irene, which immediately
exorcises the demon.

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:05.240
We’ve seen characters use incantations,
holy water, and crosses as part of the exorcism

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:08.380
process, but this is by far the most effective
and powerful method.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:12.110
Obviously, there’s gonna be a very limited
supply though, so from a balance perspective,

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:14.820
this doesn’t break the game in favor of
the good guys.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:18.420
Valak reverts back to Nun form and grabs hold
of Frenchie and after sending Irene flying

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.730
out of the room, he becomes the next victim
of Valak’s possession.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:25.580
This is the only time we see Valak possess
someone on-screen, and it’s different from

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:28.890
any of the possessions we’ve seen in other
Conjuring Universe movies.

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:32.560
The other entities possess a person by basically
puking this black stuff into their mouth,

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:35.991
I don’t really know how else to describe
it, but with Valak, we see a snake slither

00:13:35.991 --> 00:13:37.590
out of its mouth and into Frenchie’s.

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:40.320
There’s also an image of this in one of
The Duke’s books.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:43.660
The reason I bring this up, is it connects
to the idea that I mentioned earlier, that

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:47.990
the ouroboros is always associated with Valak
as a sign of the cycle of demonic possessions

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:50.230
as the demon goes from person to person.

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:53.481
All evidence points to these demons being
able to essentially split to themselves to

00:13:53.481 --> 00:13:55.230
be able to do multiple things at once.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:59.180
So while Valak was incubating inside of Frenchie’s
body, the Nun form could continue to terrorize

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:02.710
Irene and Burke, by rising out of the water
that now covered the gateway and attempting

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:04.110
to drown Irene.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:08.240
Burke tried to send the demonic entity back
to hell, but was overcome by its power; so

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:12.440
it’s ultimately Irene who tricks Valak,
by pretending to offer the holy grail, perhaps

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:16.630
the biggest bane that still threatened the
creature, and instead spitting its contents

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:21.450
onto the unholy being, causing it to be torn
apart as the gateway to hell appears to close.

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:24.870
The fact that she defeats it by spitting is
significant, because there had long been a

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:28.570
superstition in the nearby village that they
should spit on the ground whenever the cursed

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:29.990
Abbey is mentioned.

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:31.990
Sister Irene’s victory also makes sense.

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:35.680
Valak was still attacking her in its nun form,
probably not realizing that she had taken

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.050
her vows shortly before.

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:40.820
Irene was no longer afraid of this religious
commitment, so the appearance of the nun would

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:44.670
no longer intimidate her, but this wouldn’t
be the last time Valak would utilize this

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:45.670
appearance.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:49.390
The demon lies dormant inside of Frenchie’s
body, and uses it as a vessel to break free

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:51.780
out of the circle of crosses that surrounded
the abbey.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:54.750
The evil was no longer contained to a singular
location.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:58.470
It would continue to incubate within him as
he eventually settled down and got married,

00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:01.530
at which point the symptoms of his possession
made themselves noticeable.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:03.750
In 1970, help was called in.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:07.850
Frenchie is diagnosed by a pair of paranormal
investigators named Ed and Lorraine Warren.

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:11.350
Lorraine is most likely the sister, or at least a close relative of Sister

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:14.910
Irene, given that Irene is from Bridgeport,
Connecticut, the same place that Lorraine

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:15.910
was born.

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:19.090
They also both have clairvoyant visions, and
that ability seems to be hereditary.

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:21.330
Lorraine’s daughter exhibits the trait as
well.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:24.715
When Ed and Lorraine meet Frenchie, it’s
one of the worst possessions they’ve ever seen.

00:15:24.715 --> 00:15:29.040
He’s speaking in fluent Latin, despite having
a 3rd grade education and inverted crosses

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:31.220
can be seen emanating from under his skin.

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:35.120
The couple assisted on the exorcism, and since
Lorraine was a medium, it took a huge toll

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:39.500
on her, so much that she locked herself away
for 8 days and never spoke about the experience

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:40.630
for many years.

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:44.300
It’s possible that Valak wanted revenge
on the family after Irene burned it so badly

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:46.950
in Romania, and it wouldn’t be done with
them quite yet.

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:50.890
We never find out if this exorcism was successful,
but we do know that the results were grim

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:52.520
for Frenchie and his family.

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:56.930
In 1976, Lorraine has a vision containing
Valak while investigating an unrelated case

00:15:56.930 --> 00:16:00.720
in Long Island, and the experience contributed
to making it one of the most haunting cases

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:01.720
of her career.

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:07.360
“Ed, this is as close to hell as I ever
want to get.”

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:10.470
With Frenchie no longer around, Valak searched
for a new target.

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:13.870
There were probably other possessions that
took place between Frenchie’s demise in

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:18.970
1970 and the happenings in Enfield, England
in 1977, but so far they’ve not been documented

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:19.970
in any movie.

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:23.380
The best targets for a demon are those who
are weak of faith, as we learn from Sister

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:26.910
Charlotte in Annabelle Creation, and one thing
that can cause a person’s faith to weaken

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:28.740
is distress in their family life.

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:33.280
“The timing isn’t a coincidence, negative
entities often feed off of emotional distress.”

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:37.540
So Valak’s next target is the Hodgson family,
who recently lost their father when he ran

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:39.841
away and had twins with a woman from down
the street.

00:16:39.841 --> 00:16:43.310
They most likely opened themselves up to the
poltergeist when the sisters Janet and Margaret

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:45.660
used a spirit board to ask a vulnerable question.

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:48.020
“Is Dad ever coming home?”

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:51.710
As we know thanks to other Conjurverse entries,
reaching out to the spirit world to try to

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:55.800
get information or talk to a loved one can
be dangerous, because doing so is essentially

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:58.170
inviting an inhuman spirit into your life.

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:02.060
The inhuman spirit may trick the victim, making
him or her think they are talking to the spirit

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:05.230
of a person, when in fact, they’re talking
to a malevolent entity.

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:08.959
So asking if their Dad is coming home told
Valak that this family is already struggling

00:17:08.959 --> 00:17:11.990
on an emotional level, and they would be the perfect
targets.

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:16.470
But after nearly being defeated by Irene,
Valak wanted to operate in secrecy this time,

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:20.280
so instead of haunting the family directly,
it took hold of the ghost of a man named Bill

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:23.699
Wilkins, making it seem like Bill was the
one terrorizing the family.

00:17:23.699 --> 00:17:27.279
During the middle of the night, Janet is transported
downstairs in front of the chair that Bill

00:17:27.279 --> 00:17:28.500
Wilkins passed on.

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:32.909
As taught by Ed Warren, the OG Horror History
teacher before Emo Abraham Lincoln took over,

00:17:32.909 --> 00:17:35.289
there are three stages of demonic activity.

00:17:35.289 --> 00:17:37.360
“Infestation, oppression and possession.”

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:40.210
The Hodgsons began to experience the symptoms
of infestation.

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:44.746
Janet was terrorized in her dreams, and Valak
forced her to sleepwalk, sleeptalk, and Sleep

00:17:44.746 --> 00:17:45.667
Hawk.

00:17:45.667 --> 00:17:46.472
Wait, no.

00:17:46.472 --> 00:17:47.217
Not Sleep Hawk.

00:17:47.217 --> 00:17:48.550
You can go back to sleep, Sleep Hawk.

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:52.580
But Valak would do other stuff, like manifest
the image of Bill Wilkins to scare them, move

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:56.120
around toys and objects to give the impression
that these items are possessed, intimidate

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:57.743
them with voices in the night…

00:17:57.743 --> 00:17:59.293
“AAHHHHHH!!!!”

00:18:01.349 --> 00:18:03.906
...and mess with the TV, or as they called it:

00:18:03.906 --> 00:18:05.100
MORTIS MEDIA: "The telly."

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:08.889
This is also another example of Valak using
reflections to scare a victim, just like it

00:18:08.889 --> 00:18:10.519
did to Sister Irene in the chapel.

00:18:10.519 --> 00:18:14.110
At this point, the activity escalates to Stage
2: Oppression.

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:18.570
This involves shaking beds, slamming doors,
bite marks, flying furniture and other very

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.470
clear cut paranormal mayhem.

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:23.870
The family flees the house in the middle of
the night, and brings in outside help.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:28.559
Police officers, reporters, videographers,
passers by and others all experience the phenomenon.

00:18:28.559 --> 00:18:33.059
It is around this time that a strange occurrence
goes down back in the US that could suggest

00:18:33.059 --> 00:18:36.880
that we may see Valak again in a future Conjuring
installment.

00:18:46.033 --> 00:18:49.990
While Valak was making the Hodgson family
more miserable in the United Kingdom, Lorraine

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:52.470
was growing more paranoid over in the United States.

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:56.299
Ed had seen Valak in a dream, which caused
him to create a painting of the creepy nun,

00:18:56.299 --> 00:18:58.029
and Lorraine would have a vision of her own.

00:18:58.029 --> 00:19:02.019
There’s also a scene where Judy is frozen
by the disturbing image of Valak, though it’s

00:19:02.019 --> 00:19:05.520
not entirely clear if this is all part of
Lorraine’s vision, or if they were both

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:06.520
able to see Valak.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:09.790
I have the sense that Judy does see Valak
though, because the name appears multiple

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:10.940
times in her artwork.

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:13.830
Lorraine would also discover the demon’s
name in her own vision.

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:15.690
“What do you want?”

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.559
“I want my MTV!”

00:19:17.559 --> 00:19:21.549
As the Enfield Poltergeist gets more and more
attention in the media, Valak would hide behind

00:19:21.549 --> 00:19:23.730
the ghost of the old man, Bill Wilkins.

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:28.039
From my understanding of the events, it essentially
used Bill as a shield, commandeering his voice

00:19:28.039 --> 00:19:32.049
and in some cases his appearance, and this
also made it so that Valak’s demonic energy

00:19:32.049 --> 00:19:33.820
would not be picked up on by a medium.

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:37.460
Listen to the way that Janet would eventually
describe the phenomenon.

00:19:39.516 --> 00:19:41.970
“Does it feel like it’s coming from inside
you?”

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:42.970
“No.

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:45.380
It feels like it’s coming from behind me.

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:46.899
Like I’m being used.”

00:19:46.899 --> 00:19:50.889
But Bill was not the only facade that the
inhuman spirit would use to its advantage.

00:19:50.889 --> 00:19:54.730
The Hodgson’s youngest son, Billy, has a
zoetrope toy that tells the nursery rhyme

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:56.029
of The Crooked Man.

00:19:56.029 --> 00:19:59.730
Billy used to sing along with it in order
to work on improving his speech impediment,

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:01.500
but he never quite overcame it.

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:05.509
Valak tends to use the form of whatever it’s
subject has not overcome, so when Billy is

00:20:05.509 --> 00:20:07.840
alone, Valak appears to him as The Crooked
Man.

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:12.100
What’s not entirely explained is if The
Crooked Man once existed as a separate entity,

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:15.760
like Bill Wilkins, or if it was just Valak
taking the form it saw on the toy.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:19.429
I’m guessing the Crooked Man is a separate
entity though, based on this line from Ed.

00:20:19.429 --> 00:20:23.190
“The old man, the Crooked Man, they’re
just facades, trying to keep us from seeing

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:24.270
the real evil in that house.”

00:20:24.270 --> 00:20:27.299
I don’t think Valak would risk exposing
itself when it had kept its own involvement

00:20:27.299 --> 00:20:28.749
a secret for so long.

00:20:28.749 --> 00:20:32.190
The demon would not want the church finding
out and sending people in to destroy it.

00:20:32.190 --> 00:20:35.100
You’ll notice that it never uses the nun
form until Lorraine shows up.

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:39.110
The in-universe explanation is that Valak
used the nun to attack Lorraine’s faith,

00:20:39.110 --> 00:20:42.779
which was shaken by this encounter that scared
her so much all those years ago.

00:20:42.779 --> 00:20:46.009
Director James Wan explained the decision
further in an Instagram post.

00:20:46.009 --> 00:20:50.039
“During editing, I deemed this beautifully
designed/sculpted horned demon too out of

00:20:50.039 --> 00:20:51.149
left-field for the film.

00:20:51.149 --> 00:20:54.509
It needed to be more grounded and personal
— something that would take Lorraine’s

00:20:54.509 --> 00:20:56.740
faith and try to test/corrupt it.

00:20:56.740 --> 00:21:00.789
I remember the real-life Lorraine Warren talking
about her love and reverence for her nun friends,

00:21:00.789 --> 00:21:03.789
and a lightbulb went off — thus… the Demon
Nun was born.

00:21:03.789 --> 00:21:08.029
So we went back and replaced all the Horned
Demon (scenes) with the Nun during additional photography.”

00:21:08.029 --> 00:21:11.710
Many of the Hodgson’s neighbors donated
crosses that were hung up all around Janet

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:14.999
and Margaret’s room, in hopes this could
weaken the evil and prevent objects from moving

00:21:14.999 --> 00:21:18.940
around, but unlike the circle of crosses at
the abbey in Romania, this is not enough to

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:19.990
contain Valak.

00:21:19.990 --> 00:21:23.740
The case would eventually gain enough notoriety
that the church decides to send Ed and Lorraine

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:25.480
across the sea to see what’s up.

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:28.870
When they arrive, Valak remembers them, and
hopes to get Bill to scare them away.

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:31.364
“It said it wants to hurt you.”

00:21:31.364 --> 00:21:32.819
“When did it say that?”

00:21:33.289 --> 00:21:34.360
“Right now.”

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:39.250
On December 21st, 1977, they perform a test
to see if the spirit haunting the house was

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:42.510
speaking through Janet, or if she was just
making the noises on her own.

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:45.750
They’re unable to determine that it was
all Janet, but Lorraine is still skeptical

00:21:45.750 --> 00:21:47.850
because she doesn’t sense any presence in
the house.

00:21:47.850 --> 00:21:51.470
That night, Janet is transported in her sleep
to the first floor ceiling where she sees

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:53.409
old man Bill sitting on his chair.

00:21:53.409 --> 00:21:57.390
He gets up and goes upstairs, then she’s
pulled upwards into her room, the room where

00:21:57.390 --> 00:22:00.049
most of the paranormal instances had taken
place.

00:22:00.049 --> 00:22:04.129
Valak’s presence causes all of the crosses
in the room to invert, and Janet encounters

00:22:04.129 --> 00:22:07.080
old man Bill, who has the yellow glowing eyes
of the demon.

00:22:07.080 --> 00:22:10.470
Ed and Lorraine get into the room in time
to rescue Janet from being suffocated at the

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:11.759
foot of the window curtain.

00:22:11.759 --> 00:22:15.629
A day later, on the 22nd, Ed helps fix a floor
in the basement of the house, where Valak

00:22:15.629 --> 00:22:16.690
rises again.

00:22:16.690 --> 00:22:20.190
It first looks as if it’s going to attack
Ed, and I surmise this is in order to lure

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:24.220
Mrs. Hodgson into the flooded area, where
it can then attack and bite her in the arm.

00:22:24.220 --> 00:22:25.740
This attack strategy isn’t random.

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:29.270
Valak wants to freak out the family and isolate
them by making it look like they’re just

00:22:29.270 --> 00:22:30.410
making the whole thing up.

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:34.010
When Ed finds the retainer with teeth, or
as they called them in the UK, Teef, that

00:22:34.010 --> 00:22:37.090
line up with the bite mark on Peggy’s arm,
he’s going to question if it was placed

00:22:37.090 --> 00:22:41.140
there by a supernatural entity, or if it was
planted there by Peggy herself to sell the

00:22:41.140 --> 00:22:42.140
story.

00:22:42.140 --> 00:22:45.730
That is the reason Valak has everyone turn
away while Janet is making the demonic voices

00:22:45.730 --> 00:22:49.750
and the reason that the only convincing proof
of a demonic infestation happens while nobody

00:22:49.750 --> 00:22:51.799
from outside the household is present.

00:22:51.799 --> 00:22:53.820
This leads into the next part of Valak’s
plan.

00:22:53.820 --> 00:22:57.610
The house is readied up with video recording
equipment, hoping to catch some of the supernatural

00:22:57.610 --> 00:22:58.809
happenings on tape.

00:22:58.809 --> 00:23:00.070
But Valak plays it smart.

00:23:00.070 --> 00:23:03.539
It knows that it’s managed to trick Lorraine
up to this point by hiding behind the ghost

00:23:03.539 --> 00:23:07.499
of Bill Wilkins undetected, but if proof of
the poltergeist is captured, Ed and Lorraine

00:23:07.499 --> 00:23:10.429
will take it back to the church, they’ll
send in a bunch of their people, just as they

00:23:10.429 --> 00:23:11.929
did at the Abbey of St. Carta.

00:23:11.929 --> 00:23:15.970
So instead, the demon devises a plan to put
a stop to the investigation.

00:23:15.970 --> 00:23:19.980
It tells Janet she has to fake a paranormal
incident in front of the cameras, threatening

00:23:19.980 --> 00:23:22.179
to kill her family if she doesn’t comply.

00:23:22.179 --> 00:23:26.149
So she does just that, sticking knives into
the table, throwing and destroying furniture,

00:23:26.149 --> 00:23:28.379
and smashing all the dishes in the kitchen.

00:23:28.379 --> 00:23:33.090
The audio guy picks up a strange sound, which
they trace to Janet, who mangled in an electrical

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:36.280
closet, where she speaks Bill’s voice, saying
more nonsensical phrases.

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:41.330
The whole incident was recorded by a paranormal
sceptic, the psychologist named Anita Gregory, who

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:44.649
was happy to have found “proof” that the
Hodgsons were faking the haunting.

00:23:44.649 --> 00:23:48.070
Once the tape gets out, the public gains the
impression that everything was a hoax, and

00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:51.809
all the investigators and reporters clear
out, once again giving the family, and more

00:23:51.809 --> 00:23:53.960
importantly, Valak, their privacy back.

00:23:53.960 --> 00:23:57.760
Luckily for the Hodgsons, Ed figures out that
Bill Wilkins was trying to covertly send a

00:23:57.760 --> 00:24:00.580
message by overlapping the two audio recordings.

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:05.330
“Help, me, it, won’t, let, me, go!”

00:24:05.330 --> 00:24:09.260
Upon hearing this, Lorraine has another vision,
where she speaks to the real Bill Wilkins

00:24:09.260 --> 00:24:13.927
and gains an understanding of the true nature
of Valak’s presence for the first time.

00:24:22.809 --> 00:24:27.100
Lorraine has another vision, or perhaps this one
is more of an astral projection of her in

00:24:27.100 --> 00:24:30.750
the Green Street house, where she speaks to
the real Bill Wilkins, uncorrupted by the

00:24:30.750 --> 00:24:33.039
evil manipulation of Valak for the first time.

00:24:33.039 --> 00:24:37.379
He tells her that ‘he came here to see his
family, but he can’t go because “it wants

00:24:37.379 --> 00:24:38.509
her so badly”.’

00:24:38.509 --> 00:24:41.809
Breaking this down, Bill is saying he entered
the world of the spirits instead of moving

00:24:41.809 --> 00:24:45.000
on to heaven, because he thought he would
be able to see his deceased family members.

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:49.029
But he discovered they were not there, and
wanted to go on, but Valak would not let go

00:24:49.029 --> 00:24:53.509
of him, because Valak wanted to use him as
a piece of its plan to possess Janet’s soul.

00:24:53.509 --> 00:24:56.529
When Lorraine asks how to stop it, Bill leaves
her with a riddle.

00:24:56.529 --> 00:24:58.139
I am given and I am taken.

00:24:58.139 --> 00:25:01.200
I was there at your first breath,
But you didn't ask for me.

00:25:01.200 --> 00:25:03.230
But I will follow you till your death.

00:25:03.230 --> 00:25:07.200
Before she can figure it out, Valak appears
and essentially breaks up the mental connection,

00:25:07.200 --> 00:25:10.759
and this is the first time Lorraine has been
able to sense the inhuman spirit that her

00:25:10.759 --> 00:25:13.450
family member had gone up against decades
before.

00:25:13.450 --> 00:25:15.549
The answer to Bill’s riddle is: a name.

00:25:15.549 --> 00:25:19.461
A name is given at birth, a name taken by
people throughout your life to identify you.

00:25:19.461 --> 00:25:22.580
You don’t ask for a name, but it follows
you to your death.

00:25:22.580 --> 00:25:25.429
The one part of the riddle that would have
been misleading for me is the line: “I was

00:25:25.429 --> 00:25:26.669
there at your first breath.”

00:25:26.669 --> 00:25:30.070
Because that’s not always the case, I think
a lot of couples name their baby after it

00:25:30.070 --> 00:25:31.070
is born.

00:25:31.070 --> 00:25:34.087
Maybe Bill should have said, “I was there
at your first birthday party” or something.

00:25:34.087 --> 00:25:37.497
So Lorraine's realization that she needs a name to have dominion over Valak

00:25:37.497 --> 00:25:40.260
goes back to the Genesis passage that I mentioned earlier.

00:25:40.260 --> 00:25:44.257
It is man's ability to name something that gives man power over that thing.

00:25:44.257 --> 00:25:48.490
Anyway, as Ed and Lorraine rush back to the
house, Valak is now on a full-on reign of terror.

00:25:48.589 --> 00:25:52.870
Stage 2 of demonic activity is oppression,
and judging how this stage is getting worse

00:25:52.870 --> 00:25:56.779
and worse for the family, I can only assume
that Valak is getting very close to Stage

00:25:56.779 --> 00:25:57.960
3: Possession.

00:25:57.960 --> 00:26:01.940
It seems like it was even already starting
to possess Janet for short periods of time,

00:26:01.940 --> 00:26:03.059
if that’s a possibility.

00:26:03.059 --> 00:26:06.559
When the Warrens arrive, Peggy is locked out
of the house in a full state of panic.

00:26:06.559 --> 00:26:09.970
Ed tries to break in through the front window,
the demon hurls the couch across the room

00:26:09.970 --> 00:26:11.130
to block his entry.

00:26:11.130 --> 00:26:14.990
So he goes around back to go through the laundry
room and break in from under the floorboards,

00:26:14.990 --> 00:26:18.960
but once inside, Valak locks the door, effectively
separating him from Lorraine.

00:26:18.960 --> 00:26:23.029
The entity messes with the pipes and scalds
Ed’s face with piping hot water, partially

00:26:23.029 --> 00:26:26.669
blinding him, but he’s able to hobble his
way to the upstairs bedroom where Janet is

00:26:26.669 --> 00:26:31.179
about to walk out of the open window and impale
herself on the spikey tree stump that waits

00:26:31.179 --> 00:26:31.679
below.

00:26:31.679 --> 00:26:35.279
I’m not entirely sure why Valak would do
this, since we’ve kind of established that

00:26:35.279 --> 00:26:38.080
when someone dies, a demon can no longer possess
them.

00:26:38.080 --> 00:26:41.119
And it’s pretty clear that Valak’s main
goal IS to possess her.

00:26:41.119 --> 00:26:44.649
But as I have in the other videos, I’ll
attempt to justify why Valak might have behaved

00:26:44.649 --> 00:26:45.649
like this.

00:26:45.649 --> 00:26:48.710
In Annabelle, we saw in the book, The Devil’s
Welcome, that Valak and 

00:26:48.710 --> 00:26:52.480
Malthus, are just two of the
many demons detailed that all answer to Belial,

00:26:52.480 --> 00:26:54.830
who is basically the leader of all demons.

00:26:54.830 --> 00:26:58.749
We can even see Valak’s symbol, the Ouroboros,
appear way back in that movie.

00:26:58.749 --> 00:27:02.330
We’ve also seen in both Annabelle and The
Nun that summoning these demons from Hell

00:27:02.330 --> 00:27:06.159
usually involves making a human sacrifice
along with some kind of spell.

00:27:06.159 --> 00:27:10.369
Maybe this was all part of Valak’s plan
to summon another demonic presence, possibly

00:27:10.369 --> 00:27:11.369
Belial.

00:27:11.369 --> 00:27:14.129
Ed catches her before this can happen, but
this leaves him at risk to fall out of the

00:27:14.129 --> 00:27:15.129
window himself.

00:27:15.129 --> 00:27:19.590
Lorraine comes in and finds Valak standing
in the corner as Ed tries to reel in Janet.

00:27:19.590 --> 00:27:23.600
She runs to save Ed, but Valak’s scream
easily sends her flying backwards into the

00:27:23.600 --> 00:27:27.450
wall, however, she uses the demon’s name
to gain dominion over it.

00:27:27.450 --> 00:27:29.429
“You are Valak.

00:27:29.429 --> 00:27:30.760
The defiler.

00:27:30.760 --> 00:27:32.080
The profane.

00:27:32.080 --> 00:27:34.739
The marquis of snakes.”

00:27:34.739 --> 00:27:38.809
Upon saying this, Valak appears to crumble,
and when Lorraine condemns it back to hell,

00:27:38.809 --> 00:27:43.919
it breaks down even further, revealing it’s
true form to her for the first and only time,

00:27:43.919 --> 00:27:46.799
before shrinking down into a void and disappearing.

00:27:46.799 --> 00:27:50.480
This would be the last confirmed interaction
that the Warrens have with Valak, however

00:27:50.480 --> 00:27:52.929
that may not mean the character is gone for
good.

00:27:52.929 --> 00:27:57.690
As I mentioned, Valak takes on more than one
persona during the 1977 Enfield poltergeist

00:27:57.690 --> 00:28:02.240
saga, one of these facades was the manifestation
of a nursery rhyme called The Crooked Man.

00:28:02.240 --> 00:28:05.529
After many of the Warrens’ cases, they bring
home a trinket and put it in their room of

00:28:05.529 --> 00:28:06.529
cursed objects.

00:28:06.529 --> 00:28:10.720
Ed describes these objects as being bearers
of evil spirits, almost like keeping a genie

00:28:10.720 --> 00:28:11.348
in a bottle.

00:28:11.348 --> 00:28:14.610
For the Enfield case, they bring home Johnny’s
Crooked Man zoetrope.

00:28:14.610 --> 00:28:18.110
If Valak went back to hell, then then I’m
guessing The Crooked Man is the one trapped

00:28:18.110 --> 00:28:19.110
inside this toy.

00:28:19.110 --> 00:28:23.559
That seems to leave things open for another
evil do-er to stumble upon the evocation books

00:28:23.559 --> 00:28:28.159
left behind by the Duke of St. Carta and summon
Valak to once again cross the threshold and

00:28:28.159 --> 00:28:29.989
terrorize our world.

00:28:29.989 --> 00:28:33.330
Regardless of what the future holds, I’ll
be sure to cover it here.

00:28:33.330 --> 00:28:37.260
If you want to explore the complete histories
of the other entities found in the Conjuring

00:28:37.260 --> 00:28:41.690
universe go ahead and check out that playlist
on the left and remember to subscribe to CZsWorld

00:28:41.690 --> 00:28:46.659
for new horrors every week, RING the deathbell
for ALL notifications and I’ll see you in

00:28:46.659 --> 00:28:47.380
the next one.

00:28:47.380 --> 00:28:50.003
Assuming we both survive.

